Interpretation:
In an EdS spherical separate universe, Upsilon^2=1/Omega_m,local exactly.
Matter-curvature equality therefore supplies a non-fitted regional dynamical crossover at Upsilon=sqrt(2).
Inserted into the same first-passage bookkeeping, this earlier barrier lies in the variance regime needed for a volume-rich V branch on large-void scales.
Curvature domination itself is not acceleration (it is coasting/w=-1/3 in an FRW bookkeeping); the equality is tested only as a phase-selector candidate.
The calculation is not a precision cosmology fit and does not derive the vacuum free-energy density.

